// Auto-generated for the Unit Board — Level 3 (2001–3000字) Unit 6
window.T6_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"ambition – creature","cards":[{"w":"ambition","p":"n.","d":"a strong desire to do or achieve something significant; ambition","c":"雄心；抱負；志向（可數/不可數）","s":"After ten years of hard work, George finally fulfilled his lifelong ambition by opening his own international business.","t":"經過十年的辛勤奮鬥，喬治終於開辦了自己的跨國公司，實現了他畢生的抱負。"},{"w":"ambitious","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing a strong desire and determination to succeed","c":"有雄心壯志的；野心勃勃的","s":"The technology company announced an ambitious plan to reduce carbon emissions across all its factories by half.","t":"這家科技公司宣布了一項宏大的／具雄心的計畫，要在所有工廠減少一半的碳排放。"},{"w":"announce","p":"v.","d":"to make a public or formal declaration about a fact, event, or intention","c":"宣布；公布；宣告（動詞）","s":"The school principal was very pleased to announce that our baseball team had won the national championship.","t":"校長非常高興地宣布，我們學校的棒球隊贏得了全國冠軍。"},{"w":"announcement","p":"n.","d":"a public or formal statement about a fact, occurrence, or intention","c":"公告；通告；宣告（可數/不可數）","s":"Passengers at the crowded train station listened carefully to the public announcement about the delayed express train.","t":"擁擠火車站內的乘客們仔細聆聽有關特快列車延誤的公共廣播通告。"},{"w":"declare","p":"v.","d":"to say something in a solemn, emphatic, or official manner","c":"宣告；正式聲明；申報（動詞）","s":"Unable to pay his heavy mounting debts after losing his job, Gary was forced to declare bankruptcy in court.","t":"失業後無法償還日益增加的沉重債務，蓋瑞被迫在法庭上宣告破產。"},{"w":"brake","p":"n.","d":"a device for slowing or stopping a moving vehicle, typically by friction","c":"煞車；制動器（可數）","s":"When a stray dog suddenly ran onto the road, the driver slammed on the brake to avoid hitting it.","t":"當一隻流浪狗突然跑上馬路時，駕駛猛踩煞車以避免撞上牠。"},{"w":"brake","p":"v.","d":"to slow down or stop a vehicle using a brake","c":"煞車；減速（動詞）","s":"Driving instructors advise students to brake slowly and steadily whenever a traffic light turns from green to yellow.","t":"駕訓班教練建議學生，每當交通號誌由綠燈轉為黃燈時都要緩緩煞車。"},{"w":"bubble","p":"n.","d":"a thin sphere of liquid enclosing air or another gas","c":"氣泡；泡沫；泡泡（可數）","s":"The happy young children giggled joyfully as they blew colorful soap bubbles in the sunny backyard garden.","t":"開朗的年幼孩子們在陽光明媚的後院花園裡吹著五彩繽紛的肥皂泡泡，開心地咯咯笑。"},{"w":"bubble","p":"v.","d":"to form or produce bubbles; to rise to the surface","c":"冒泡；起泡；沸騰（動詞）","s":"Nancy saw the fresh chicken soup begin to bubble gently in the pot, so she added the noodles.","t":"南西看見鍋裡的新鮮雞湯開始緩緩冒泡沸騰，便把麵條放了進去。"},{"w":"bubbly","p":"adj.","d":"full of bubbles; lively and cheerful in personality","c":"充滿氣泡的；活潑開朗的","s":"Jessica is popular among her classmates because she has an energetic and bubbly personality that brightens the room.","t":"潔西卡在同學中很受歡迎，因為她擁有活力充沛且活潑開朗的性格，總能讓房間充滿歡樂。"},{"w":"clay","p":"n.","d":"a stiff, sticky fine-grained earth that can be molded when wet and baked","c":"黏土；陶土（不可數）","s":"Art students sat around the rotating wheel in the pottery studio to shape wet clay into beautiful vases.","t":"美術系學生圍坐在陶藝工作室的旋轉拉胚機旁，將濕陶土／黏土塑造成美麗的花瓶。"},{"w":"comparison","p":"n.","d":"a consideration or estimate of the similarities or dissimilarities between two things","c":"比較；對照；比擬（可數/不可數）","s":"The history teacher asked each student to make a thorough comparison between the American and French revolutions.","t":"歷史老師要求每位學生在美國革命與法國革命之間進行深入的比較。"},{"w":"compare","p":"v.","d":"to estimate, measure, or note the similarity or dissimilarity between","c":"比較；對照；比作（動詞）","s":"Smart consumers usually check online reviews to compare prices and quality before purchasing electronic devices.","t":"精明的消費者在購買電子產品前，通常會查看網路評價來比較價格與品質。"},{"w":"comparable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be likened to another; similar in quality or importance","c":"可比較的；比得上的；相當的","s":"The imported local olive oil is of comparable quality to the expensive French brands but sells for half the price.","t":"這款進口的當地橄欖油品質與昂貴的法國品牌相當／比得上，但售價只有一半。"},{"w":"concert","p":"n.","d":"a musical performance given in public by several performers or of several works","c":"音樂會；演唱會（可數）","s":"Thousands of excited teenage fans screamed when their favorite rock band walked onto the stage at the concert.","t":"當最喜愛的搖滾樂團走上演唱會舞台時，數千名興奮的青少年粉絲發出尖叫。"},{"w":"creature","p":"n.","d":"an animal, as distinct from a human being; a living being","c":"生物；動物；生靈（可數）","s":"Uncle Robert is a true creature of habit who always eats the exact same breakfast at seven.","t":"羅伯特叔叔是一個道地的生活習慣固定者／依循習慣之人，總是在七點整吃一模一樣的早餐。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"drip – further","cards":[{"w":"drip","p":"v.","d":"to fall in small drops of liquid, or to let liquid fall in drops","c":"滴下；漏水；淌（動詞）","s":"As the white candle burned quietly on the dining table, melted wax dripped down its sides.","t":"當白色蠟燭在餐桌上靜靜燃燒時，融化的蠟油順著兩側滴了下來。"},{"w":"drip","p":"n.","d":"a small drop of liquid that falls, or the sound of falling drops","c":"水滴；滴水聲；點滴注射（可數）","s":"We could hardly fall asleep in the old wooden cabin because of the constant drip of rain on the tin roof.","t":"因為鐵皮屋頂上持續不斷的雨水滴答聲，我們在老舊的小木屋裡幾乎無法入睡。"},{"w":"drugstore","p":"n.","d":"a shop that sells medicines, cosmetics, toiletries, and daily goods","c":"藥妝店；雜貨藥局（可數）","s":"Whenever David catches a slight cold, he walks down the street to the local drugstore to buy fever medicine.","t":"每當大衛輕微感冒時，他都會走到街上的當地藥妝店購買退燒藥。"},{"w":"pharmacy","p":"n.","d":"a store or hospital dispensary where medicinal drugs are prepared and sold","c":"藥局；調劑室（可數）","s":"After finishing his medical checkup at the clinic, Mr. Adams went to the nearest pharmacy to pick up his prescription pills.","t":"在診所完成健康檢查後，亞當斯先生前往最近的藥局領取他的處方藥丸。"},{"w":"dumb","p":"adj.","d":"unable to speak (dated); stupid or foolish in informal modern usage","c":"啞的；說不出話的；愚蠢愚笨的","s":"The shocking news of the sudden earthquake left the entire newsroom completely struck dumb for several seconds.","t":"突然發生地震的震驚消息讓整個新聞編輯室足足好幾秒驚訝得說不出話來／啞口無言。"},{"w":"echo","p":"n.","d":"a sound caused by the reflection of sound waves from a surface","c":"回音；反響；共鳴（可數）","s":"When the energetic hiker shouted loudly at the top of the mountain peak, a clear echo bounced back from the cliffs.","t":"當充滿活力的登山者在山頂大聲呼喊時，懸崖峭壁間傳來一聲清晰的回音。"},{"w":"echo","p":"v.","d":"to repeat or resound with an echo; to repeat someone's words or feelings","c":"發出回音；迴響；附和（動詞）","s":"The cheerful laughter of playing children echoed loudly through the empty hallways of the quiet school building.","t":"玩耍孩童們歡快的笑聲在安靜校舍空曠的走廊裡響亮地迴盪。"},{"w":"elbow","p":"n.","d":"the joint between the forearm and the upper arm","c":"手肘；肘部（可數）","s":"Cleaning the rusty metal fence took several hours and required a great deal of hard elbow grease.","t":"清理生鏽的金屬柵欄花了數小時，需要付出極大的力氣苦功。"},{"w":"engage","p":"v.","d":"to occupy or attract someone's interest; to participate in","c":"吸引；參與；從事；訂婚（動詞）","s":"The experienced science teacher used interactive games and fun experiments to engage the curious students in the lesson.","t":"那位經驗豐富的理化老師運用互動遊戲與趣味實驗，在課堂上吸引好奇學生的注意力。"},{"w":"engaged","p":"adj.","d":"having agreed to marry someone; busy or occupied with a task","c":"訂婚的；忙於…的；通話中的","s":"David and Karen announced that they had gotten engaged after dating happily for more than four years.","t":"大衛與凱倫在甜蜜交往四年多之後，宣布他們已經訂婚了。"},{"w":"engagement","p":"n.","d":"an agreement to marry someone; a formal arrangement to do something","c":"訂婚；約定；公務會約（可數）","s":"The happy young couple celebrated their official engagement by hosting an intimate dinner party for their families.","t":"這對幸福的年輕伴侶透過為雙方家庭舉辦溫馨的晚宴，來慶祝他們的正式訂婚。"},{"w":"exhibition","p":"n.","d":"a public display of works of art or items of interest","c":"展覽；展覽會；展現（可數/不可數）","s":"The national museum opened a magnificent exhibition displaying ancient gold treasures discovered along the Silk Road.","t":"國家博物館開辦了一場宏偉的展覽，展出沿著絲路發現的古代黃金珍寶。"},{"w":"exhibit","p":"v.","d":"to publicly display a work of art or item in an art gallery or museum","c":"展出；展覽；顯現出（動詞）","s":"Many talented local sculptors will exhibit their unique marble artworks at the annual summer craft festival.","t":"許多才華橫溢的在地雕塑家將在一年一度的夏季工藝節上展出他們獨特的大理石藝術品。"},{"w":"farther","p":"adj./adv.","d":"at, to, or by a greater physical distance","c":"更遠的；較遠地（指實體物理距離）","s":"The weary travelers were completely exhausted and felt they could not walk even one meter farther in the snow.","t":"疲憊的旅人們精疲力竭，覺得自己連在雪地中再多走遠一點的力氣都沒有了。"},{"w":"further","p":"adj./adv.","d":"to a greater degree or extent; additional","c":"進一步的；更深一層的；此外","s":"If you require any further information about our master degree program, please contact the admissions office.","t":"如果您需要關於我們碩士學程的任何進一步資訊，請洽詢招生辦公室。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"fond – mobile","cards":[{"w":"fond","p":"adj.","d":"having an affection or liking for someone or something","c":"喜愛的；深情的；溺愛的","s":"Jenny is extremely fond of her playful new puppy and spends hours tossing balls with it in the yard.","t":"珍妮非常喜愛她那隻貪玩的新小狗，每天花好幾個小時在院子裡跟牠玩拋球。"},{"w":"gossip","p":"n.","d":"casual or unconstrained conversation about other people, often involving rumors","c":"八卦；閒言碎語；愛說長道短的人（不可數/可數）","s":"Mature coworkers should focus on their professional duties instead of wasting valuable time spreading idle gossip.","t":"成熟的同事應該專注於自己的專業職責，而不是浪費寶貴時間散播無聊的閒言碎語。"},{"w":"gossip","p":"v.","d":"to engage in casual talk about the private affairs of others","c":"說長道短；閒聊八卦（動詞）","s":"It is very unfair and unkind to gossip behind someone's back without knowing the complete truth.","t":"在不知全貌的情況下在別人背後說長道短，是非常不公平且不友善的。"},{"w":"grin","p":"v.","d":"to smile broadly, showing one's teeth","c":"露齒而笑；咧嘴笑（動詞）","s":"The friendly little boy grinned broadly at the kind mailman who handed him a birthday package.","t":"那個友善的小男孩對著遞給他生日包裹的親切郵差燦爛地咧嘴露齒笑。"},{"w":"grin","p":"n.","d":"a broad smile showing the teeth","c":"露齒微笑；咧嘴的笑容（可數）","s":"Doug flashed an evil grin that made everyone in the room suspect he was planning a silly practical joke.","t":"道格臉上閃過一抹邪氣的咧嘴微笑，讓房間裡的每個人都懷疑他正在策劃一場惡作劇。"},{"w":"hopeful","p":"adj.","d":"feeling or inspiring optimism about a future event","c":"抱有希望的；充滿希望的","s":"Despite facing severe financial difficulties, the dedicated small business owners remain hopeful that sales will recover soon.","t":"儘管面臨嚴重的財務困境，那些敬業的小企業主依然抱有希望，相信業績很快就會復甦。"},{"w":"hopeless","p":"adj.","d":"feeling or causing despair; having no expectation of good","c":"絕望的；毫無希望的；糟透的","s":"Lost in the freezing wilderness without food or a map, the frightened hikers began to feel completely hopeless.","t":"在酷寒的荒野中迷路且沒有食物或地圖，受驚嚇的登山客們開始感到徹底絕望。"},{"w":"inform","p":"v.","d":"to give someone facts or information; to tell","c":"通知；告知；使了解（動詞）","s":"The airline sent a text message to inform passengers of the sudden gate change well before boarding.","t":"航空公司在登機前發送簡訊告知乘客登機門臨時變更。"},{"w":"informative","p":"adj.","d":"providing useful or interesting information; instructive","c":"長見識的；提供豐富資訊的","s":"The visiting professor gave a highly informative lecture that helped students understand the complex history of global trade.","t":"客座教授發表了一場內容豐富長見識的演講，幫助學生理解全球貿易的複雜歷史。"},{"w":"journey","p":"n.","d":"an act of traveling from one place to another, especially over a long distance","c":"旅程；旅行；歷程（可數）","s":"Learning a foreign language fluently is an exciting lifelong journey that requires constant practice and patience.","t":"流利學習一門外語是一段令人興奮的終身歷程，需要不斷的練習與耐心。"},{"w":"meanwhile","p":"adv.","d":"in the intervening period of time; at the same time","c":"在此期間；與此同時（副詞）","s":"Carl has a formal job interview scheduled for next Friday; meanwhile, he will continue to practice his speaking skills.","t":"卡爾排定下週五有一場正式的工作面試；在此期間／與此同時，他將繼續練習口說技巧。"},{"w":"mobile","p":"adj.","d":"able to move or be moved freely or easily; capable of moving","c":"行動的；可移動的；便於活動的","s":"The municipal government established a mobile library bus that brings children's storybooks to remote mountain villages.","t":"市政府設立了一輛行動圖書館巴士，將兒童故事書載運到偏遠山村。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"normal – purify","cards":[{"w":"normal","p":"adj.","d":"conforming to a standard; usual, typical, or expected","c":"正常的；一般的；標準的","s":"On a normal weekday, Mr. Peterson leaves for the office at seven in the morning and returns home at six.","t":"在平常正常的工作日，彼得森先生早晨七點出門去辦公室，晚上六點返家。"},{"w":"abnormal","p":"adj.","d":"deviating from what is normal or usual, typically in a way that is undesirable","c":"不正常的；反常的；異常的","s":"The alert doctor ordered further blood tests after noticing an abnormal increase in the patient's white cell count.","t":"機警的醫生在注意到該病患的白血球數量異常增加後，安排了進一步的血液檢查。"},{"w":"onion","p":"n.","d":"a swollen edible bulb with a pungent taste and smell, composed of several layers","c":"洋蔥（可數）","s":"Whenever Vincent chops an onion into tiny pieces on the kitchen cutting board, his eyes begin to tear up.","t":"每當文森在廚房砧板上將洋蔥切碎時，他的眼睛就會開始流淚。"},{"w":"ox","p":"n.","d":"a castrated bull used as a draft animal; plural form is oxen","c":"牛；閹公牛（複數為 oxen）","s":"In traditional agricultural villages, hardworking farmers relied heavily on a sturdy ox to pull heavy wooden plows.","t":"在傳統農業村落中，勤勞的農民極度依賴一頭強壯的牛／閹牛來拉動沉重的木犁。"},{"w":"pal","p":"n.","d":"a close friend or companion; a buddy","c":"朋友；夥伴；哥們（可數）","s":"During her elementary school years, Emily regularly exchanged handwritten letters and stamps with her Canadian pen pal.","t":"在小學時期，艾美經常與她的加拿大筆友互相寄送手寫信件與郵票。"},{"w":"pancake","p":"n.","d":"a thin, flat cake of batter, fried on both sides on a griddle or in a frying pan","c":"煎餅；薄煎餅；美式鬆餅（可數）","s":"On relaxed Sunday mornings, my mother loves to cook a tall stack of warm fluffy pancakes topped with maple syrup.","t":"在輕鬆的星期天早晨，我母親喜歡煎一整疊淋上楓糖漿的熱騰騰鬆軟薄煎餅／鬆餅。"},{"w":"peel","p":"v.","d":"to remove the outer covering or skin from a fruit, vegetable, or object","c":"削皮；剝皮；脫皮（動詞）","s":"The chef asked the kitchen assistant to peel ten large potatoes before placing them in the boiling water.","t":"主廚要求廚房助手在將馬鈴薯放入滾水中之前，先削去十顆大馬鈴薯的皮。"},{"w":"peel","p":"n.","d":"the outer skin of certain fruits and vegetables, especially citrus","c":"果皮；蔬菜外皮（可數/不可數）","s":"The pastry baker added finely grated lemon peel to the cake batter to give it a refreshing citrus aroma.","t":"西點烘焙師在蛋糕麵糊中加入磨碎的檸檬皮，使其帶有清爽的柑橘香氣。"},{"w":"postpone","p":"v.","d":"to arrange for something to take place at a time later than originally scheduled","c":"延期；推遲；延緩（動詞）","s":"Because a massive tropical typhoon was approaching the coast, tournament organizers decided to postpone the outdoor marathon until next month.","t":"由於一場強大的熱帶颱風逼近海岸，賽事主辦單位決定將戶外馬拉松延期到下個月。"},{"w":"postponement","p":"n.","d":"the action of postponing something; an act of rescheduling to a later date","c":"延期；推遲；延緩措施（可數/不可數）","s":"The CEO's sudden illness unfortunately led to the indefinite postponement of the crucial international trade negotiations.","t":"執行長突發的重病遺憾地導致了這場關鍵國際貿易談判的無限期延期。"},{"w":"pure","p":"adj.","d":"not mixed or adulterated with any other substance or material; innocent","c":"純淨的；純粹的；純真的","s":"Natural spring water originating high in the snowy mountains is completely pure and perfectly safe to drink.","t":"源自高聳雪山的天然山泉水完全純淨，可以直接安全飲用。"},{"w":"purify","p":"v.","d":"to remove contaminants from; to make ceremonially or spiritually clean","c":"淨化；提純；使純潔（動詞）","s":"The modern filtration plant uses advanced ultraviolet technology to purify river water before pumping it to homes.","t":"這座現代化濾水廠在將河水輸送到住戶前，利用先進的紫外線技術淨化水質。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"relief – suburban","cards":[{"w":"relief","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of relaxation following release from anxiety, distress, or pain","c":"寬慰；如釋重負；救濟物資（不可數）","s":"When the doctor announced that the medical test results were completely negative, Helen let out a deep sigh of relief.","t":"當醫生宣布醫學檢驗結果完全為陰性時，海倫發出了一聲深深的如釋重負／寬慰的嘆息。"},{"w":"relieve","p":"v.","d":"to ease or reduce pain, distress, or difficulty","c":"緩解；減輕；使解脫（動詞）","s":"Drinking a cup of warm chamomile tea before bedtime can effectively help to relieve daily mental stress.","t":"睡前喝一杯溫熱的洋甘菊茶，能有效幫助緩解日常的精神壓力。"},{"w":"staff","p":"n.","d":"all the people employed by a particular organization or business","c":"全體全職員工；教職員（集合名詞）","s":"The friendly and attentive hotel staff welcomed our exhausted tour group warmly upon our late arrival.","t":"友善且周到的飯店全體員工在我們深夜抵達時熱情地歡迎了我們這群疲憊的旅行團。"},{"w":"stir","p":"v.","d":"to move a spoon or stick through a liquid; to arouse strong emotions","c":"攪拌；攪動；激起；煽動（動詞）","s":"Jane used a wooden spoon to stir the bubbling tomato soup continuously so it would not burn in the pot.","t":"珍用木匙持續攪拌滾沸的番茄濃湯，以免它在鍋底燒焦。"},{"w":"stir","p":"n.","d":"a slight physical movement, or a commotion and widespread excitement","c":"攪拌一下；轟動；騷動（可數）","s":"Before drinking your freshly brewed milk tea, be sure to give it a quick stir with the plastic straw.","t":"在喝現煮奶茶之前，務必用塑膠吸管快速攪拌一下。"},{"w":"suffer","p":"v.","d":"to experience or be subjected to something bad or unpleasant","c":"遭受；受苦；蒙受（損失）（動詞）","s":"Throughout the humid summer vacation, poor Arthur was suffering from severe allergies and frequent sneezing.","t":"在整個潮濕的暑假期間，可憐的亞瑟一直受…所苦於嚴重的過敏症與頻繁打噴嚏。"},{"w":"suffering","p":"n.","d":"the state of undergoing pain, distress, or hardship","c":"痛苦；苦難；折磨（不可數/可數）","s":"International charitable organizations dispatch medical teams and relief supplies to relieve human suffering in war-torn regions.","t":"國際慈善機構派遣醫療隊與救濟物資，以緩解飽受戰爭蹂躪地區的人民疾苦／痛苦。"},{"w":"tricky","p":"adj.","d":"requiring care and skill because difficult or awkward; deceitful","c":"棘手的；難辦的；狡詐狡猾的","s":"The final chemistry exam included a very tricky bonus question that only three students in the entire class solved correctly.","t":"化學期末考包含了一道非常棘手難解的加分題，全班只有三位學生正確解出。"},{"w":"trick","p":"n.","d":"a cunning act or scheme intended to deceive or outwit someone; a skillful act","c":"把戲；惡作劇；竅門；戲法（可數）","s":"On Halloween night, excited neighborhood children dressed in costumes love to play a silly trick on their neighbors.","t":"在萬聖節之夜，穿著特殊服裝的興奮社區孩童喜歡對鄰居進行滑稽的惡作劇／把戲。"},{"w":"urban","p":"adj.","d":"relating to, characteristic of, or situated in a city or town","c":"城市的；都市的；城鎮的","s":"Rapid economic modernization has prompted millions of rural workers to migrate toward large urban centers in search of jobs.","t":"快速的經濟現代化促使數百萬鄉村勞工遷往大型都市／城市中心以尋找工作機會。"},{"w":"rural","p":"adj.","d":"relating to, characteristic of, or situated in the countryside rather than the town","c":"鄉村的；田園的；農村的","s":"After spending thirty stressful years working in downtown skyscrapers, the retired couple chose to live in a quiet rural village.","t":"在市中心摩天大樓度過充滿壓力的三十年職場生涯後，這對退休夫婦選擇定居在寧靜的鄉村小村莊。"},{"w":"suburban","p":"adj.","d":"relating to or characteristic of a suburb; residential area near a city","c":"郊區的；近郊的","s":"Many young families prefer to purchase modern houses in suburban neighborhoods where streets are quiet and parks are safe for children.","t":"許多青年家庭更喜歡在郊區的住宅區購買現代化住宅，那裡街道寧靜且公園對孩子來說很安全。"}]}];
